  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) is strong at 0.591, while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 0.208. Avgpool clearly beats transformer for aggregation (0.591 vs 0.519). Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multimodal fusion adds value on top of the already-strong RNA signal, or whether the weak image channel is merely noise that degrades performance. This experiment (config_018: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests whether combining the best-known RNA configuration with the available image encoder yields any benefit over RNA-only. It uses the best-validated settings for each component (pca_n2000 + avgpool for RNA, resnet50 for image) and the simplest fusion (concat), isolating the fusion question. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information experiment: if multimodal helps, we justify investing remaining runs in better image encoders (ViT-L) and fusion strategies; if it does not, we redirect effort toward improving the RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt). Either outcome sharply narrows the search space."
}

